mmit_sha":"9434ab808b5a61620aecd7f6ee2e3fb2b2a3f528","position":"1787092345686553001-6235328e-05f2-4935-b3a2-92d9cec3ac30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ca572226ddc104451f9106548ab40cb47755c7bb411bb2cee1183206b15f256","event_uuid":"bcc5c723-b6f4-43a0-99e0-82d96a617785","position":{"commit_sha":"bee86e0c28acbc204cd59808d965be1396d2d277","position":"1787092634928979493-bcc5c723-b6f4-43a0-99e0-82d96a617785"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (confirmed; fast path): docs/event-schema.md:51 statically enumerates six LINK relations and omits `caused_by`, while the same sentence explicitly cites `graph/_links.py:CANONICAL_RELATIONS`; src/rebar/graph/_links.py:17-34 contains seven canonical relations including `caused_by` and states it is directional, non-blocking, and never cycle-inducing. The closed design/implementation authority `isogonal-wedded-catfish` (0b96-cbcb-0ea2-479d) explicitly required docs/event-schema.md to document the seventh relation and defines those semantics; docs/ticket-model.md:148-160 and :189-194 already publish them. History discriminates the mechanism: commit 901241b218 added `caused_by` to code/help/ticket-model but did not modify docs/event-schema.md; later commit 693a6bf412 rewrote the LINK/UNLINK row and retained the six-value inventory. Therefore the changeable root cause is a stale manually duplicated inventory in docs/event-schema.md, not a runtime relation defect. Legitimacy: defect/incomplete implementation against the closed 0b96 design authority. Expected repair is docs-only semantics restoration plus a contract test tying the maintained event-schema LINK row to the canonical relation set; no caller behavior depends on the omission.","timestamp":1787091657072731001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final debug report (pre-push)\n\nProblem: `docs/event-schema.md` omitted the supported `caused_by` LINK relation and its semantics.\n\nProven root cause: the relation inventory is manually duplicated. Commit 901241b218 added `caused_by` to CANONICAL_RELATIONS, schema/types, help, and ticket-model surfaces but did not edit `docs/event-schema.md`; commit 693a6bf412 later rewrote that row and retained the six-value list. The maintained row therefore drifted from the cited source `src/rebar/graph/_links.py:CANONICAL_RELATIONS`. Closed authority `isogonal-wedded-catfish` explicitly required event-schema documentation and specifies directional, non-blocking, non-cycle-inducing semantics. Classification: incomplete-implementation/defect, not a new capability.\n\nProof: before repair, the contract parsed the real LINK/UNLINK row and compared it with CANONICAL_RELATIONS; it failed deterministically with `missing=[caused_by], extra=[]`, ruling out a runtime relation defect or extra stale documentation value.\n\nTest: `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py` was finalized and observed RED before the docs edit (1 collected, 1 executed, assertion failure for sole missing relation). It is GREEN after repair. Exact-defect mutation removing only `caused_by` from the repaired inventory returned the same test to RED with the same sole-missing diagnostic; restoring the repair returned the focused contract suite GREEN. The equality assertion is order-independent, so relation reordering/refactoring does not trip it. No separate fixer agent was used because doing so would consume the concurrency slot reserved for the ongoing macOS deadline investigation.\n\nFix: the LINK inventory now includes `caused_by`; the row explicitly states it is directional, non-blocking, and non-cycle-inducing, and includes it among non-blocking relations permitted for session_log endpoints.\n\nScope and safety: docs plus one documentation contract only; no runtime behavior, dependency, or existing test changed. The omission has no behavioral dependents. Focused event-schema contracts: 5 passed. `make lint`: PASS. `make typecheck`: PASS (560 source files). `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\nSibling sweeps: construct sweep over maintained docs/package inventories found no other six-relation inventory after this repair. Parity rule: every maintained relation inventory must equal CANONICAL_RELATIONS. CLI help, generated CLI reference, schema/types, library facade, and MCP facade already contain/test `caused_by`; automated callers use the shared graph core; dual-direction N/A because `caused_by` is intentionally directional. No missing parity slot remains.\n\nResidual risk: the row remains hand-maintained, but the new set-equality contract prevents future additions from silently omitting any canonical relation. No other observed fragility remains.\n\nReplication: the original report no longer reproduces; parsing the maintained event-schema row yields the complete canonical seven-relation set and the required `caused_by` semantics are present.","timestamp":1787092314434784001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1877 (patch set 1), commit 4ec33564f4bc67f79e5fd8595e865758434b0aec, Change-Id I3e51afc84331b5b8ae3391c363230195766a9d56. Local terminal evidence: focused event-schema contract suite 5 passed; exact omission mutation reproduced RED with sole missing relation caused_by; restored GREEN; make lint passed; make typecheck passed (560 source files); git diff --check passed; commit hook passed; DCO, Change-Id, and canonical rebar-ticket trailer verified. Awaiting independent Gerrit LLM-Review and Verified gates; not submitted or closed.","timestamp":1787092345686553001}],"created_at":1787091229521723001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"537c876b-19f8-4154-ab41-7b48484e89a1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b6e1-c217-8cd3-4446"},{"link_uuid":"bcc5c723-b6f4-43a0-99e0-82d96a617785","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e364-0f50-f625-4101"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit review of change 1874 observed that `docs/event-schema.md` lists six canonical LINK relations but omits the already-supported `caused_by` relation. The packaged CLI overview lists `caused_by`, and closed task `isogonal-wedded-catfish` is the design/implementation authority adding it as the seventh directional, non-blocking, non-cycle-inducing relation.\n\n## Investigation and repair plan\n\n- Reproduce the maintained-documentation mismatch against current `origin/main` and cite the authoritative implementation/design surfaces.\n- Under rebar-debug, prove whether the omission is a stale inventory rather than a runtime defect.\n- Add a held-out documentation contract that parses the LINK/UNLINK row and requires set equality with `rebar.graph._links.CANONICAL_RELATIONS`, preventing any future relation omission; retain an explicit `caused_by` semantics assertion as this bug's RED anchor.\n- Repair only the proven documentation omission, run exact-defect mutation, focused documentation gates, lint, and typecheck.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- Run `pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py` before the repair and require set equality to fail specifically with `caused_by` missing from the documented inventory.\n- Run the same command after the repair and require it to pass.\n- Remove `caused_by` from the repaired event-schema row, rerun the focused test, require RED, then restore the repair.\n- Run `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the focused documentation-contract suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` includes `caused_by` in the canonical LINK relation inventory.\n- [ ] The parsed event-schema LINK inventory equals `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` as a set.\n- [ ] The event-schema relation prose states `caused_by` is directional.\n- [ ] The event-schema relation prose states `caused_by` is non-blocking and non-cycle-inducing.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py` is RED before repair with `caused_by` as the sole missing canonical relation.\n- [ ] The same focused test is GREEN after repair.\n- [ ] The exact omission mutation returns the focused test to RED.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"restore the omitted caused_by relation and its directional/non-blocking/non-cycle semantics"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py","reason":"documentation contract pinning the LINK inventory to the implemented canonical relation set"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e364-0f50-f625-4101"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"05f07262-88c6-47b6-90ff-c60fcf3e30c3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["docs","links","parity"],"ticket_id":"6532-9285-1808-40ea","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Document caused_by in the event-schema relation inventory","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["361f2e57-3